licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Changes relative to oliverbestmann/webgpu (fork base: commit b087960 on its
main branch):

- Module path renamed from github.com/oliverbestmann/webgpu to
  github.com/belluikit/webgpu. Every import of the module's own packages was
  updated (examples/, wgpu/, wgpuglfw/, cmd/enums/, the generated header of
  wgpu/gen_enums.go).
- go.mod requires the platform library modules
  github.com/belluikit/webgpu/libs-{android,darwin,ios,linux,windows} from this
  repository's libs-* branches instead of oliverbestmann's, and drops the
  upstream retract directive.
- libs-ios branch: adds an arm64 iOS Simulator slice
  (libs-ios/arm64-simulator/libwgpu_native.a, from the same wgpu-native
  release) selected by the `iossimulator` build tag.
- libs-windows branch: replaces the arm64 MSVC library (wgpu_native.lib) with
  a GNU-ABI (gnullvm) build, libs-windows/arm64/libwgpu_native.a, which the
  llvm-mingw toolchain used by cgo on windows/arm64 can link. It is built by
  the added workflow .github/workflows/build-wgpu-windows-arm64.yml.
- libs-* branches: module paths renamed to belluikit, and each branch carries
  wgpu-native's license notice (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
- update-wgpu.sh targets this repository instead of oliverbestmann's.
- README rewritten to describe this fork.

The prebuilt static libraries on the libs-* branches are from wgpu-native
(https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu-native), licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. Apart
from the two slices above they are upstream's release archives, unchanged.
